# =============================================================================
# cloud-init meta-data (NoCloud) - Linux guests
# =============================================================================
# Proxmox generates a meta-data file of its own; supplying this one overrides it
# with `cicustom meta=`.
#
# WHY BOTHER OVERRIDING IT
#   For instance-id. cloud-init treats instance-id as the identity of the machine:
#   if it changes between boots, cloud-init decides this is a new machine and
#   re-runs its "per-instance" modules. Left to Proxmox, the value is derived in a
#   way this repository does not control, which makes "will cloud-init run again
#   after I rebuild this VM?" a question with no answer in the code.
#
#   Pinning it to the VM name plus its VMID makes the answer explicit and readable:
#   the identity is the machine's identity in lab.yaml, and it changes only when the
#   machine itself does.
#
# NOT USED ON WINDOWS. Cloudbase-Init reads a configdrive2 drive whose metadata
# Proxmox generates, and Proxmox already fills the hostname in there correctly. An
# override would be one more thing to keep in sync for no gain.
#
# Generated for: ${hostname}
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
instance-id: ${instance_id}
local-hostname: ${hostname}
